{#
| Variable                  | Type   | Description                                    |
|---------------------------|--------|------------------------------------------------|
| component                 | object | merchant settings from twilight.json           |
| component.image           | string | the banner — fills the whole card              |
| component.alt             | string | image description for SEO / screen readers     |
| component.fixed_height    | bool   | uniform card height instead of the image's shape |
| component.height          | int    | desktop card height in px, when fixed           |
| component.focus           | mixed  | which part survives the crop, when fixed        |
| component.show_cta        | bool   | overlay a button on the image                  |
| component.button_text     | string | CTA label                                      |
| component.button_url      | string | CTA link                                       |
| component.button_position | mixed  | one of 9 grid slots, e.g. "bottom-center"      |
| position                  | int    | sorting block                                  |

The uploaded image IS the banner — no text column, no panel background. The
only optional chrome is one CTA, placed on a 3×3 grid.

── Two sizing modes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DEFAULT: the card takes the artwork's own aspect ratio, so nothing is ever
cropped. This is what a banner with text baked into the image needs — a fixed
490px card against a 2.95:1 file trimmed ~5% off each side under `cover` and
ate the Arabic headline.

FIXED: the merchant wants every banner the same height regardless of upload.
Cropping is then unavoidable, so `focus` chooses which part of the artwork
survives instead of always trimming the edges.

Salla hands `component.image` back as a bare URL with no dimensions, so the
ratio cannot be known at render time — the inline script below reads it off
the decoded image and writes it to --qib-ratio. `naturalWidth` is checked
first because a cached image can already be complete before the load handler
is attached, which would leave the card stuck on its fallback ratio forever.

The overlay grid runs LTR on purpose: postcss-preset-env downlevels logical
properties assuming LTR, so "يمين/يسار" are mapped to physical right/left in
CSS. The button re-isolates its own RTL for the Arabic label.
#}
{% if component.image %}
    {# dropdown-list values arrive as a list (and sometimes as option objects) —
       unwrap to the plain slot string, matching how bareq handles the format #}
    {% set pos = component.button_position is iterable ? component.button_position|first : component.button_position %}
    {% set pos = pos.value|default(pos)|default('bottom-center') %}

    {% set focus_raw = component.focus is iterable ? component.focus|first : component.focus %}
    {% set focus = focus_raw.value|default(focus_raw)|default('center') %}

    {% set fixed = component.fixed_height %}

    {% set css = '' %}
    {% if fixed %}
        {% set h = component.height|default(490) %}
        {% set css = '--qib-height: ' ~ h ~ 'px;'
                   ~ '--qib-height-md: ' ~ (h * 0.82)|round ~ 'px;'
                   ~ '--qib-height-sm: ' ~ (h * 0.61)|round ~ 'px;'
                   ~ '--qib-focus: ' ~ focus ~ ';' %}
    {% endif %}

    <section class="s-block qibanner{{ fixed ? ' qibanner--fixed' : '' }}"
             id="qibanner-{{ position }}"
             {% if css %}style="{{ css }}"{% endif %}>
        <div class="container">
            <div class="qibanner__box"{% if not fixed %} data-qib-box{% endif %}>
                <img class="qibanner__img"
                     src="{{ component.image }}"
                     alt="{{ component.alt|default(component.button_text)|default('') }}"
                     loading="lazy"/>

                {% if component.show_cta and component.button_text and component.button_url %}
                    <div class="qibanner__overlay" data-pos="{{ pos }}">
                        <a class="qibanner__btn" href="{{ component.button_url }}">{{ component.button_text }}</a>
                    </div>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    {% if not fixed %}
        <script>
        (function () {
            var box = document.querySelector('#qibanner-{{ position }} [data-qib-box]');
            if (!box) { return; }
            var img = box.querySelector('.qibanner__img');
            if (!img) { return; }

            function applyRatio() {
                if (!img.naturalWidth || !img.naturalHeight) { return; }
                box.style.setProperty('--qib-ratio', img.naturalWidth / img.naturalHeight);
            }

            // A cached image may already be decoded before this runs, in which
            // case 'load' never fires again — check up front, then listen.
            if (img.complete) { applyRatio(); }
            img.addEventListener('load', applyRatio);
        }());
        </script>
    {% endif %}
{% endif %}
